-- A `/proc` scan skips a process only when it is shown to be gone: its stat read fails with `NotFound` or `ESRCH`, or an unparseable stat line (an exiting process can yield an empty or truncated one; a line without the kernel's trailing newline counts as truncated) is followed by a re-read that does. A process whose stat stays unparseable is an error, never an empty group.
